# motoquencer `bulkedit`, button lane. motoquencer.md: the bulk edit fires "if you
# move one fader (or encoder) or touch/press one button" — so the touch plates are
# in scope too, each step to the right taking "the same value".
#
# "The same value" is read as the RESULTING value of the pressed step (gate on or
# off), not as a toggle applied to every step: a toggle would flip the steps that
# already agreed with the edit, which is the opposite of "the same value".
#
# Step 3's gate is switched off first with bulkedit LOW (gates 1 1 1 0). Then CTRL
# is held and step 1's plate is pressed: step 1 goes off and steps 2 and 3 COPY
# that off — step 3, already off, stays off (a toggle would have turned it back
# on). Pressing step 1 again with CTRL still held stamps the gates back on.
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[m4]
[motoquencer]
    clock       = I1
    bulkedit    = I2
    numsteps    = 4
    numfaders   = 4
    quantize    = 0
    cvbase      = 0
    cvrange     = 1
    holdcv      = 0
    buttonmode  = 0
    defaultgate = 1
    gate        = O2
>>>
# bulkedit low: switch step 3's gate off on its own.
@0 set I2 0
@1 touch F4 1
@2 touch F4 0
# hold bulkedit, press step 1's plate: 1 goes off, 2 and 3 copy "off".
@3 set I2 1
@4 touch F2 1
@5 touch F2 0
# play: gate on step 0 only.
@6 set I1 1
@6 expect O2 1 tol 1e-4
@7 set I1 0
@8 set I1 1
@8 expect O2 0 tol 1e-4
@9 set I1 0
@10 set I1 1
@10 expect O2 0 tol 1e-4
@11 set I1 0
@12 set I1 1
@12 expect O2 0 tol 1e-4
@13 set I1 0
# press step 1's plate again, CTRL still held: 1 goes on and 2, 3 copy "on".
@14 touch F2 1
@15 touch F2 0
@16 set I1 1
@16 expect O2 1 tol 1e-4
@17 set I1 0
@18 set I1 1
@18 expect O2 1 tol 1e-4
@19 set I1 0
@20 set I1 1
@20 expect O2 1 tol 1e-4
@21 set I1 0
@22 set I1 1
@22 expect O2 1 tol 1e-4
@23 set I1 0
